// P3E.1 (test-drive.md TD3.1 Label…, TD3.3 Labels, TD3.7 labels column, TD3.8 labels in the
// details panel; derived-and-linking ER1.2 Labels location), against
// `test-drive/lesson-documents-page.png`: the documents page with 8 seeded documents.
// 01 Create ▾ open, the pointer on Label….
// 02 Create label dialog, "Fixtures" typed.
// 03 created: the toast with Undo.
// 04 two more labels (Hardware from the Label button, Medical Devices): the settings menu's
//    Labels ▸ lists them.
// 05 right-click › Properties… on a row: the modal with the thumbnail, Owner, Document
//    description and Document labels (search field, three checkboxes, Create new label),
//    Created by.
// 06 "har" typed in Search labels: only Hardware is left.
// 07 Hardware checked: the Labels column appears in the list with the Hardware chip, and the
//    chip under Document labels.
// 08 the row menu's Labels ▸ submenu on another document (Fixtures hovered): each label with its
//    colour dot, a check mark on those the document has.
// 09 Fixtures given to two more documents from the menu: the Labels column.
// 10 settings › Labels ▸ Fixtures: only the 3 documents with Fixtures; caption "FIXTURES".
// 11 the caption's ⋯: Rename… / Delete….
// 12 Rename label dialog → "Jigs".
// 13 renamed: the caption and chips read Jigs.
// 14 Delete… confirmation ("taken off 3 documents").
// 15 deleted: back to the documents, the chips gone.
// 16 Ctrl+Z: Jigs back on its 3 documents.
// 16b the grid view: the cards carry their label chips.
// 16c the list: Motor mount selected, then moved to the trash: the selection is cleared.
// 16d the Trash: Motor mount's Properties… are read-only (description and labels shown, not
//     editable; "restore it to edit"). Then Ctrl+Z restores it.
// 17 (ER1.2) a document opened by double-click → Assembly 1 → Insert → Other documents: the
//    locations list the labels (Hardware, Jigs, Medical Devices) after the folders.
// 18 the Jigs location: its documents.
